course: dictionary
lesson: 4698
title: Honesty: telling the truth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Honesty means telling the truth, not cheating, and not stealing. It is one of the good habits that people admire most. «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage; vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty.» So honesty is a virtue, and greed is a vice.
explain: Honesty also means being open about your feelings and your mistakes. If you break something and own up to it, you are being honest, even when it is hard. Honesty builds trust, so people can believe you next time.
explain: Being honest can still be kind. «When someone sincerely asks for honest feedback, kind, polite honesty helps them.» You can tell the truth gently, without being hurtful. Ask yourself: is my truth kind as well as true?
fact: Honesty is being truthful, not lying, cheating or stealing.
fact: Honesty also means being open about your feelings and your mistakes.
fact: «Honesty is the best policy» means that being honest pays off in the end.
fact: Honesty builds trust, and trust helps friendships and families to last.
fact: Honesty and kindness work well together: you can tell the truth without being hurtful.
exercise: What does honesty mean? | Keeping every secret from your friends | Winning every game you play | *Telling the truth and not cheating or stealing | Being loud and confident in class
exercise: «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage.» What kind of habit is honesty? | A kind of food | A bad habit | *A good habit | A sport
exercise: Which word is NOT in this list: «effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage»? | kindness | courage | skill | *greed
test: Owning up when you break something, even when it is hard, is an example of what? | *honesty | cheating | cruelty | greed
test: «Honesty is the best policy» means what? | Honesty is a type of cake | *Being honest pays off in the end | You should always lie to win | Policies are only for offices
exam: In a story, an honest woodcutter tells the truth about his axe and is rewarded. What does the reader learn? | Lies always win in the end | Woodcutters become rich quickly | Axes are dangerous, so never carry one | *Honest people are often rewarded, and lies cause trouble
